Q: Multiple headers in HTML A: <p>One way to obtain your desired behaviour is to make the <code>header</code> <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/position#sticky" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>sticky</code></a> and checking wheter the user had scrolled or not. To achieve this, we can use <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/scrollTop" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>element.scrollTop</code></a>. More specifically, we can use something like <code>body.scrollTop</code> to see how far the user has scrolled.</p>
<p><strong>N.B.</strong> Keep in mind that <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/7436602/10301322">some browsers' rendering mode do not fully support <code>document.body.scrollTop</code></a>, thus you could resort to <code>document.documentElement.scrollTop</code>.</p>
<p>Following a simple example:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const l = document.getElementById("Logo");
document.addEventListener('scroll', () =&gt; {
  // browser inclusivity
  if (document.body.scrollTop &gt; 10 || document.documentElement.scrollTop &gt; 10) {
    l.classList.add('hide');
  } else {
    l.classList.remove('hide');
  }
});</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>header {
  background-color: #0097A7;
  color: #ffffff;
  padding: 2%;
  text-align: center;
  /* Making the header sticky */
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
}

h1 {
  font-size: 270%;
  margin: 2% 0;
}

nav {
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, .4);
  border-radius: 25px;
  width: 50%;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
  font-family: 'Neuton', serif;
  font-weight: bold;
}

nav a {
  color: #fff;
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 100%;
  font-weight: bold;
  padding: 1% 4%;
}

nav a:hover {
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, .4);
  box-sizing: border-box;
  border-radius: 25px;
}

.hide {
  display: none;
}</code></pre>
