<p>The above code use the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/scroll_event" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>scroll event</code></a> to trigger a simple check aimed to add or remove the class <code>.hide</code> responsable to &quot;toggle&quot; the element <code>h1</code>.</p>
<p>It's easy to see that I was simply &quot;hiding&quot; the <code>h1</code> element containing the logo, but obviously this concept can be expanded in almost any way.</p>

Q: Why is my PHP query string malfunctioning? A: <p>I would recommend you to study the official documentation on Increment/Decrement Operators:</p>
<p><a href="https://www.php.net/manual/en/language.operators.increment.php" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://www.php.net/manual/en/language.operators.increment.php</a></p>
<p>For example, you may note that for $a++ (Post-increment), it returns $a, then increments $a by one</p>
<p>So the following:</p>
<pre><code>$x=10;
echo $x++;
</code></pre>
<p>will display 10 (echo $x++) , but then $x is 11</p>
<p>See something like this: <a href="https://onlinephp.io/c/85c38" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://onlinephp.io/c/85c38</a></p>
<p>Now, in your code, you may wish to</p>
<ol>
<li><p>avoid using the same variable $cardNumber when calculating the &quot;next card&quot; and &quot;previous card&quot; (e.g. use two new variables, like $nextcardNumber and $precardNumber)</p>
</li>
<li><p>unless you are familiar with the increment/decrement operators, otherwise simply consider using +1 / -1 to do the job</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>So simply use something like:</p>
<pre><code>$nextcardNumber = $cardNumber+1;
$precardNumber = $cardNumber-1;
</code></pre>
<p>So the code will become:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;?php
if (isset($deck_id)) {
  // Get deck_id from URL query string
  $deck_id = $_GET[&quot;deck_id&quot;];
} else {
  $deck_id = 0;
}

if (isset($cardNumber)) {
  // Work out which card to show, using cardNumber from URL query string
  $cardNumber = $_GET[&quot;cardNumber&quot;];
} else {
  $cardNumber = 0;
}
?&gt;


&lt;?php

$nextcardNumber = $cardNumber+1;
$precardNumber = $cardNumber-1;

?&gt;

&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;!-- Submit button has hidden field to decrease value of cardNumber --&gt;
  &lt;form action=&quot;view_cards.php&quot; method=&quot;get&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;hidden&quot; name=&quot;deck_id&quot; value=&quot;&lt;?php echo $deck_id; ?&gt;&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;hidden&quot; name=&quot;cardNumber&quot; value=&quot;&lt;?php echo $precardNumber; ?&gt;&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Previous Card&quot;&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;

  &lt;!-- Submit button has hidden field to increase value of cardNumber --&gt;
  &lt;form action=&quot;view_cards.php&quot; method=&quot;get&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;hidden&quot; name=&quot;deck_id&quot; value=&quot;&lt;?php echo $deck_id; ?&gt;&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;hidden&quot; name=&quot;cardNumber&quot; value=&quot;&lt;?php echo $nextcardNumber; ?&gt;&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Next Card&quot;&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;  
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
